{"id": "EUVD-2026-90881", "enisaUuid": "c3068e71-1726-32c0-a70d-3cacabb57381", "description": "Fortra BoKS Manager contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the custom TLS ClientHello parser used by boks_portmux. A remote unauthenticated attacker can submit a malformed ClientHello and terminate boks_portmux. Although the daemon is normally restarted automatically, repeated requests can sustain the service interruption.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T15:09:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T16:02:49", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://www.fortra.com/security/advisories/product-security/fi-2026-016"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h5vq-j79p-4xf3", "CVE-2026-79896"], "assigner": "Fortra", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "945356a4-c545-33c3-bab9-f7f375650efc", "product": {"name": "BoKS Manager", "vendor": {"name": "Fortra"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0.0 \u22649.0.0.6"}, {"id": "cdbfc167-5457-3556-8a51-779e0710b13e", "product": {"name": "BoKS Manager", "vendor": {"name": "Fortra"}}, "product_version": "8.1.0.0 \u22648.1.0.23"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "29b4d7c7-dc5c-3b91-9253-65dafaf813ed", "vendor": {"name": "Fortra"}}], "isExploited": false}